  "instructions": "## Different sizes, one block\n\nA university campus has the block `10.1.0.0/22` (1024 addresses) and needs:\n\n| Network | Hosts needed |\n|---|---|\n| Students | 300 |\n| Staff | 100 |\n| Labs | 50 |\n| Link between R1 and R2 | 2 |\n\nWith **variable-length subnet masks** you give each network only as much as it needs. Allocate the largest network first, starting at the beginning of the block, then the next largest, and so on, with no gaps.\n\n## Do this\n\n1. Work out the four subnets in CIDR form (for example `10.1.0.0/23`) and type them on the right.\n2. The routers' LAN interfaces are already addressed. Click **R1** and **R2** and give their `s0` interfaces the two usable addresses of the link subnet.\n3. Ping R2 from R1 and press **Check my network**.",
