  "hints": [
    "300 hosts need 9 host bits (2^9 - 2 = 510), so Students is a /23. 100 hosts need 7 bits (/25); 50 need 6 bits (/26); 2 need 2 bits (/30).",
    "Students takes 10.1.0.0 to 10.1.1.255. Staff starts at 10.1.2.0, Labs at 10.1.2.128, and the link at 10.1.2.192.",
    "A /30 has four addresses: .192 is the network, .193 and .194 are the hosts, .195 is the broadcast."
